#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""CAD-426: deterministic split of tests/integration.rs into per-area binaries.

Reads tests/integration.rs and writes:

  - tests/common/mod.rs   — the shared harness: every item used by more than
                            one area plus all type/impl/mod declarations,
                            promoted to `pub` so binaries see them through
                            `use common::*`.
  - tests/<area>.rs       — one test binary per area: its #[test] fns and any
                            helper no other area references.
  - tests/split-map.toml  — manifest mapping every test fn and helper to its
                            binary (regenerated; do not hand-edit).

Placement of a test is decided by, in order:

  1. PINNED        — the reviewed cut carried forward from the original split
                     (favcrm/cadence PR #267) plus explicit assignments for
                     tests main added since;
  2. PREFIX_RULES  — first matching regex on the test name;
  3. SECTION_RULES — first matching regex on the `// ---- <section> ----`
                     marker that introduces the test;
  4. otherwise the test lands in tests/unplaced.rs and the script fails.

Running it again on a newer main reproduces the same layout for every test
it knows and files new ones by the rules. Run from the repo root:

    scripts/split-integration-tests            # regenerate + remove source
    scripts/split-integration-tests --check    # verify outputs are current

Two assertions in the old file were baked to the binary name `integration`
and are rewritten verbatim by TEXT_EDITS (see the comments there). The
gitleaks allow-markers on the synthetic PEM fixtures travel the same way.
"""

